LOK: AutoFilter takes the first row as header without asking

When Calc cannot tell a header from the data (a whole column of text,
an empty column), turning on AutoFilter asks whether the first row is
a header. Under LOK the client closes the box as soon as it opens,
inside the callback that announces it; the box's async handler then
applies the filter on a half-built dialog, and the next tile paint
crashes the process (GitHub ElyOffice #4). LOK asks no question here:
the first row heads the range, which is the box's default answer and
what Excel does.

--- a/sc/source/ui/view/dbfunc.cxx
+++ b/sc/source/ui/view/dbfunc.cxx
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <scitems.hxx>
+#include <comphelper/lok.hxx>
 #include <sfx2/bindings.hxx>
 #include <vcl/svapp.hxx>
 #include <vcl/weld.hxx>
@@ -340,7 +341,13 @@
